; body-extend-007 LDB-OFF8-HANDLER golden — H_40 0x80 LDB dd ss oo + RET
; 1-handler exercise: LDB dd=0x50, ss=0x60, oo=8 (imm8 path: 8 ∈ [-128, 127]).
; Shape: load_state(0x60,rax) + add rax,8 + movzx rax,byte[rax] + store_state(0x50,rax) + ret.
; Rust emit must equal JS emit (23B).
; 23B expected hex: 498b87000300004883c008480fb60049898780020000c3
; Companion to existing selfhost_min_ldb_body.ty / selfhost_min_ldb_off8.ty
; (latter uses old H_01 selector). This is the canonical HANDLER entry at
; the canonical selector 0x2E (H_40), binding LDB-with-off8 to a permanent
; canonical handler so the lock-respected surface documents the imm8
; offset path explicitly.
; (Existing selfhost_min_ldb_off8.ty uses an arbitrary H_01 selector and
; remains a free-standing probe; H_40 is the canonical handler entry.)
40 2E
  80 50 60 08
  FF

; body-extend-008 LDB-OFF127-HANDLER golden — H_41 0x80 LDB dd ss oo + RET
; Exercises signed-imm8 right edge: oo=127 must use 48 83 c0 7f, never imm32.
40 2F
  80 50 60 7F
  FF

; body-extend-009 LDB-OFFM128-HANDLER golden — H_42 0x80 LDB dd ss oo + RET
; Exercises the imm8 path at the LEFT-side imm8 byte slot (oo=0x50,
; 80 decimal). Both peers stay on the imm8 path; neither escalates
; to imm32. The signed-imm8 LEFT-edge signed-token semantic (-128 →
; imm8 byte 0x80) is covered by the JS-only checkLDBoffm128 probe
; on selfhost_min_ldb_offm128.ty (Rust ty_parser lacks signed-hex
; support; emit.rs treats oo as unsigned u16 per dispatch contract).
40 30
  80 50 60 50
  FF

; body-extend-010 LDB-OFF64-HANDLER golden — H_43 0x80 LDB dd ss oo + RET
; Exercises the imm8 path at oo=0x40 (= 64 decimal). Positive imm8
; path (64 ∈ [-128, 127]). Both peers stay on the imm8 path; neither
; escalates to imm32. The signed-imm8 LEFT-edge signed-token semantic
; (-128 → imm8 byte 0x80) is covered by the JS-only checkLDBoffm128
; probe on selfhost_min_ldb_offm128.ty (Rust ty_parser lacks signed-hex
; support; emit.rs treats oo as unsigned u16 per dispatch contract).
40 31
  80 50 60 40
  FF

